From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 17:10:52 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] iio: qcom_smgr: route the remaining samp_freq paths by data
 type

Two leftover instances of the same defect family already fixed for the
report-completion race and the samp_freq read/write path: unconditional
use of data_types[0] where the SECONDARY data type also needs handling.

1. qcom_smgr_probe()'s sample-rate init loop already walks every data
   type of a sensor by index j (data_type_count is 1 or 2), but
   dereferenced `data_types->cur_sample_rate` /
   `data_types->max_sample_rate` -- the pointer decaying to element 0
   every iteration -- so SECONDARY (e.g. prox/light's ambient-light
   channel, pressure's die-temperature channel) never got its
   cur_sample_rate initialised past its zeroed default. Index by
   data_types[j], matching what the loop already iterates over. There
   is no iio_dev or channel yet at this point in probe
   (qcom_smgr_register_sensor() runs after this loop), so there is
   nothing to route by -- looping over data types directly is the
   correct shape here, not the chan->scan_index routing used elsewhere.

2. qcom_smgr_iio_read_avail()'s IIO_CHAN_INFO_SAMP_FREQ case returned
   priv->samp_freq_vals, whose max slot was set once at registration
   from sensor->data_types[0].max_sample_rate -- always PRIMARY's rate,
   even when the SECONDARY channel (which can have a different max
   rate) asked for its own available range. Unlike probe, read_avail()
   does have a channel to route by, so apply the same
   qcom_smgr_secondary_scan_index()-based routing already used in
   read_raw/write_raw for this same attribute, filling in the max slot
   for the requesting channel's data type. The stale PRIMARY-only
   assignment at registration is removed since it is now always
   overwritten before use.

IIO_CHAN_INFO_SCALE is not an instance of this bug:
qcom_smgr_iio_read_raw()'s SCALE case dispatches purely on chan->type
(IIO_PRESSURE/IIO_TEMP vs. default), never on sensor->data_types[], so
PRIMARY and SECONDARY channels already get independent scale handling
by construction.

Signed-off-by: Giuseppe Maggio <jertlok@proton.me>
---
 drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c | 30 ++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 26 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
index 2c9dabc38a0a..0a5598d84988 100644
--- a/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
+++ b/drivers/iio/common/qcom_smgr/qcom_smgr.c
@@ -1029,9 +1029,16 @@ static int qcom_smgr_iio_read_avail(struct iio_dev *iio_dev,
 				    long mask)
 {
 	struct qcom_smgr_iio_priv *priv = iio_priv(iio_dev);
+	struct qcom_smgr_sensor *sensor = priv->sensor;
+	int sec, data_type;
 
 	switch (mask) {
 	case IIO_CHAN_INFO_SAMP_FREQ:
+		/* sec == -1 for event-only sensors too; both PRIMARY then. */
+		sec = qcom_smgr_secondary_scan_index(sensor->type);
+		data_type = (sec >= 0 && sec == chan->scan_index)
+			    ? SNS_SMGR_DATA_TYPE_SECONDARY : SNS_SMGR_DATA_TYPE_PRIMARY;
+		priv->samp_freq_vals[2] = sensor->data_types[data_type].max_sample_rate;
 		*type = IIO_VAL_INT;
 		*vals = priv->samp_freq_vals;
 		*length = ARRAY_SIZE(priv->samp_freq_vals);
@@ -1611,9 +1618,13 @@ static int qcom_smgr_register_sensor(struct qcom_smgr *smgr,
 	priv = iio_priv(iio_dev);
 	priv->sensor = sensor;
 
+	/*
+	 * samp_freq_vals[2] (max) is per-channel -- PRIMARY and SECONDARY
+	 * can have different max rates -- so it is filled in by
+	 * qcom_smgr_iio_read_avail() for the requesting channel, not here.
+	 */
 	priv->samp_freq_vals[0] = 1;
 	priv->samp_freq_vals[1] = 1;
-	priv->samp_freq_vals[2] = priv->sensor->data_types[0].max_sample_rate;
 
 	iio_dev->name = qcom_smgr_sensor_type_device_names[sensor->type];
 	iio_dev->info = &qcom_smgr_iio_info;
@@ -1688,9 +1699,20 @@ static int qcom_smgr_probe(struct qrtr_device *qdev)
 				smgr->sensors[i].id);
 
 		for (j = 0; j < smgr->sensors[i].data_type_count; j++) {
-			/* Default to maximum sample rate */
-			smgr->sensors[i].data_types->cur_sample_rate =
-				smgr->sensors[i].data_types->max_sample_rate;
+			/*
+			 * Default to maximum sample rate. There is no channel
+			 * to route by yet -- iio_dev doesn't exist until
+			 * qcom_smgr_register_sensor() below -- but there
+			 * doesn't need to be: this loop already walks every
+			 * data type this sensor has (PRIMARY and, where
+			 * present, SECONDARY) by index j, so init each one's
+			 * own rate directly instead of indexing through the
+			 * data_types pointer, which always decays to element
+			 * 0 and left SECONDARY's cur_sample_rate at its
+			 * zeroed init value.
+			 */
+			smgr->sensors[i].data_types[j].cur_sample_rate =
+				smgr->sensors[i].data_types[j].max_sample_rate;
 
 			/*
 			 * Worth keeping the range and rate: this is how the
